  "qualification_limits": [
    "Recovery occurs on the next explicit native launch; no production service restart or fallback switch is integrated.",
    "Automatic reconciliation requires a fully prepared schema-2 journal from the same boot.",
    "Legacy, cross-boot, partially prepared, temporary, corrupt, mismatched, live-owner, pinned or otherwise ambiguous journals block startup.",
    "Old kernels with unclassifiable nsfs bind pins conservatively block recovery.",
    "Saved or enumerated process IDs are never signaled during reconciliation; old jobs are not replayed.",
    "Reboot, power-loss and cross-boot recovery were not tested.",
    "These acceptance runs do not update prior CPU, memory or startup comparisons."
